  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 205 PM MDT Sun Aug 23 2026\n\nAnother multi-day break in the monsoon is underway. 18Z RAOBS\nplace the subtropical high right in between ABQ and EPZ, with \nboth recording 500mb heights of 5980m. Additional horrid stats \nfrom EPZ include a temperature of -4C at 500mb (in the middle of \na sharp inversion, and a PWAT of 0.84 inches. \n\nMeanwhile, at the surface, dewpoints have mixed out into the\nmid-30s across much of the lowlands, including LRU, ALM, and DNA.\n\nHRRR still holds out hope for a few isolated convective showers\nwith maybe some thunder over the Gila or Sacramento Mountains, \nand radar shows a few minimal blips west of the Black Range. But \ncoverage will be very minimal. \n\nTemperatures should still top out around 101-103 at ELP, with\nsimilar temperatures tomorrow. Ensembles suggest we'll peak on\nTuesday with a high around 104-106. \n\nRecord highs for ELP the next few days rise slowly with the\nforecast, but are still within range.\n\nSun 23 - 103 (2024) // fcst 102 \nMon 24 - 102 (1993) // fcst 102 \nTue 25 - 104 (2002) // fcst 104 \nWed 26 - 106 (2019) // fcst 103 \nThu 27 - 103 (2019) // fcst 102\n\nThe subtropical ridge will drift east over the next couple of days\nbefore slowly retracing its steps, then settling closer to the\nAZ/NM border by Wednesday. This will allow for northerly flow\naloft to develop, bringing weak disturbances and some recycled\nupper level moisture into the area, increasing the risk of\nthunderstorms again. Low level moisture will struggle to recover\nuntil Thursday, so lowland precip chances will lag the higher\nterrain.\n\nTemperatures will hover near or just above 100 through the rest \nof the month. Our record for number of days in August with highs \n100+ at El Paso currently sits at 20 (set in 2020). We have a \nshot at beating this record.",
